## Context

M2 transcribes the one held scan without a text layer, the Vietnamese plan
decision (Decision 458, 23 pages), and every statement it yields names the
transcription as its method. No ticket carried this. Normative text,
accepted specification v1 (tag `jetp-spec-v1`):

- `docs/jetp-extraction.md` § 6.4 (transcription: a recogniser text layer,
  two vision-capable hosted readers of different families blind to each
  other under the protocol of § 6.3, every item to the arbiter, the method
  named uncalibrated); § 13 (the M2 slice); § 15 (the check "A decision is
  held only as a scan").
- `docs/jetp-collection.md` § 8 and § 11 "M2 before the campaign": a
  born-digital copy is searched for first, and the search recorded.
- `docs/jetp-operation.md` § 5 (transcription readers, hosted, within the
  per-document budget, never for a `local_only` document).

The recogniser's text layer is an adapter (format dimension, [[1508]]); the
reading is the reading lane. Blocked by [[1508]] (text layer), [[1509]]
(the § 6.3 protocol it runs under) and [[1874]] (budgets and hosted-call
settings: both readers and the arbiter are hosted).

## Exit criteria

- [ ] The search for a born-digital copy of Decision 458 is recorded; if one is found it is registered and extracted instead, and this ticket closes on that
- [ ] A recogniser produces a text layer of the scan, cached by hash and adapter version
- [ ] Two vision-capable hosted readers of different makers read the page images and that layer blind to each other; every item goes to the arbiter; every statement names the transcription method and version, a locator with page index and page-normalised region, a likelihood and a confidence
- [ ] The run report and the coverage report name the method uncalibrated
- [ ] Pilot on a stratified sample of pages (page kind × table or prose, size stated) passes a quality check by a cross-model checker, findings recorded here, before the full 23 pages (pilot rule, [[1500]])
- [ ] Spend stays within the per-document budget (operation § 7.2)
- [ ] `make jetp-ledger-check`, `make check-fast` and `make lint` pass
